    schema:datePosted "2026-08-31"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "<h3><strong>About Engineered Arts</strong></h3> <p>Engineered Arts is the leading manufacturer of full-size humanoid robots used for entertainment, education and communication. With 20 years of hardware and software development, our robots have been sold in over 30 countries worldwide with customers such as NASA, PwC, Meta and many more.</p> <p>Our Ameca robot is well known as 'the face of AI' and a social media viral success, taking advantage of the generative AI craze. Along with our ultra-realistic Mesmer range of animated figures our robots continue to surprise and excite visitors at museums, theme parks, visitor attractions and trade shows as well as aid leading universities with AI and robotics research. Our robots are poised to break into the future mega-expansion service robot segment, with applications such as front of house, receptions, check-in desks, information points and PoS. We are also exploring how our humanoid robot technology can disrupt other robotics sectors such as the growing cobot sub-segment of the industrial robotics market.</p> <p>We are a team of dedicated engineers and creatives striving to develop the very best experiences for our customers. Our internal motto is 'Be Wow', everything we do is fun, entertaining or surprising to encounter. We always push the boundaries of what is possible in humanoid robotics, researching and developing new systems and techniques to further their appeal. We explore and challenge the human perception of robots as well as the fear and discomfort and the excitement and joy life-like mechanical humanoids present.</p> <h3><strong>About You</strong></h3> <p>Are you a seasoned sales professional ready to own and shape the revenue strategy for mid-market and enterprise customers across the UK and globally? As an Account Executive, you'll take full ownership of the sales process—from strategic prospecting through to close—while bringing the credibility and consultative depth to engage senior stakeholders at complex, high-value accounts.</p> <p>This is a quota-carrying role with real influence. You'll not only convert qualified opportunities into signed deals, but also help define how we go to market, mentor SDRs, and build the kind of long-term customer relationships that drive repeat business and global word-of-mouth. If you thrive on selling something genuinely unlike anything else on the market, this is your opportunity.</p> <h3><strong>What You'll Do and How You'll Have an Impact</strong></h3> <ul> <li>Own and drive the full sales cycle from strategic discovery through negotiation and close on high-value, complex deals</li> <li>Develop and execute account plans across a portfolio of mid-market and enterprise targets in the UK and internationally</li> <li>Partner closely with SDRs to convert qualified leads into proposals, while independently generating pipeline from target verticals and robot applications</li> <li>Lead executive-level conversations and present tailored, consultative solutions to senior decision-makers</li> <li>Deliver compelling live and virtual product demonstrations that translate cutting-edge robotics into clear business value</li> <li>Maintain rigorous pipeline management and forecasting accuracy in CRM with high data hygiene</li> <li>Act as a trusted advisor to prospects and customers, navigating complex buying committees and addressing technical and commercial objections</li> <li>Collaborate cross-functionally with marketing, product, operations, and support teams to ensure seamless customer outcomes</li> <li>Represent Engineered Arts at global trade shows, conferences, and customer site visits—becoming a credible voice in the humanoid robotics space</li> <li>Provide market intelligence and feedback to inform product roadmap and go-to-market strategy</li> </ul> <h3><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h3> <ul> <li>7–10+ years of experience in a full-cycle B2B sales role, with a strong track record of closing complex, high-value deals</li> <li>Proven success selling physical technology products, hardware, or emerging technology solutions to mid-market and enterprise customers</li> <li>Demonstrated ability to navigate long-cycle, multi-stakeholder enterprise deals while managing shorter transactional opportunities simultaneously</li> <li>Executive presence and the ability to build credibility quickly with C-suite and senior decision-makers</li> <li>Exceptional communication, consultative selling, negotiation, and relationship-building skills</li> <li>Strong commercial acumen with experience managing and accurately forecasting a substantial pipeline</li> <li>Proficiency with CRM tools (e.g. Salesforce, HubSpot) and a disciplined approach to data hygiene</li> <li>Comfortable operating in a fast-moving, innovative environment where the product category is still being defined</li> </ul> <h3><strong>Why You'll Love This Job</strong></h3> <ul> <li>Join a company where creative ambition meets engineering excellence—and where no two deals are ever the same</li> <li>Make a measurable, global impact—see your work installed and experienced in museums, theme parks, universities and boardrooms around the world</li> <li>Enjoy competitive compensation, uncapped earning potential, and flexible work arrangements that support work–life balance</li> <li>Be part of a pioneering team at the forefront of one of the most exciting technology categories on the planet</li> </ul> <p><em>At AppDirect, we believe that innovation thrives in an environment that houses diversity of excellence, experience and thought. We respect each person as their own fingerprint; unique with no one alike. We foster an environment of inclusion without regard to race, religion, age, sexual orientation, or gender identity. As such, we strongly encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, racialized people, people with disabilities, people from gender and sexually diverse communities, and/or people with intersectional identities.</em></p> <p><em>By applying to this role, you acknowledge that your application information — including your resume, contact details, and any materials you submit — may be shared with our client (the hiring organization) for the purpose of evaluating your candidacy. We act as a recruiting partner on behalf of this client. Your information will be used solely in connection with this opportunity and handled in accordance with applicable privacy laws.</em></p> <p><em>At AppDirect we take privacy very seriously. For more information about our use and handling of personal data from job applicants, please read our Candidate Privacy Policy. For more information of our general privacy practices, please see AppDirect Privacy Notice: </em><a href=\"https://www.appdirect.com/about/privacy-notice\"><em>https://www.appdirect.com/about/privacy-notice</em></a><em>&nbsp;</em></p> <p><em>At AppDirect, AI tools may assist our recruitment team with administrative automations — always under human oversight. AI tools do not make hiring decisions or solely automated decisions about your candidacy — all decisions are made by our people. By submitting your application, you acknowledge that your information may be processed in this way. You may request access or deletion at any time by contacting ----- <p>&nbsp;</p> Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow" ;
