    schema:datePosted "2026-09-01"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "SAMSUNG SDS Smart Logistics (part of the SAMSUNG Group) was founded in 2012 and is one of the fastest-growing logistics service providers in the world. As one of the most innovative companies in the industry, we offer our customers optimized solutions as well as consulting in the field of Supply Chain Management, based on our proprietary transport and warehouse management software, \"Cello.\" SAMSUNG SDS Smart Logistics operates in 40 countries worldwide and employs more than 4,500 logistics experts. At our Eschborn location, we are looking for System Administrator to support our warehouse! Tasks Administration of Linux and MS Windows based servers & services Installation and setup of web applications and database servers Setting up customer applications 1st, 2nd & 3rd level support for customer servers, web applications, databases Monitoring, analysis and reporting of performance and volume of the server infrastructure Experience with web stack technologies (HTTP, web servers, reverse proxy, load balancing) Strong understanding of OS-level security (Linux/Windows) Setup and administration of Oracle, MySQL, PostgreSQL and MSSQL databases Build, Manage, and optimize containerized environment using Docker Automate configuration management, deployment, and orchestration using Ansible Ensuring the integrity and security of systems and applications through the strict technical implementation of internal security guidelines Regular reporting according to the respective escalation level based on the problem management metric Execute backup operations, including monitoring, failure resolution, and periodic restore testing and validation Maintain technical documentation and operational procedures Perform OS patching, firmware updates, and system upgrades as per schedules Ensure timely service restoration and effective communication during incidents Requirements Successfully completed studies in computer science or a comparable qualification Several years of professional experience as a system administrator (7-10 years) Ability to work in an international, multicultural company Good experience working with cloud computing platforms such as AWS, MS Azure or Google Cloud or OCI - Very good knowledge of at least one of the following operating systems: RHEL, MS Windows Server, Docker and Ansible Solid administration knowledge in at least one of the following: MSSQL, MariaDB/MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle DB Good knowledge of VMware vSphere and shared storage Knowledge of DNS, LDAP, AD and Remote Services and SSH Experience in automation and scripting Efficient troubleshooting skills Good understanding of network fundamentals (e.g. TCP/IP, routing, subnetting, DNS, firewall) Good language skills in English (spoken and written), German desirable. Ability to work in a team and structured work complete your profile Work Authorization: A valid work authorization for Germany is required for this position. We are currently unable to provide visa sponsorship or support work permit applications. German Pay Transparency Act: We are committed to equal pay and reward qualification, experience and performance entirely independent of gender. Classification is based exclusively on objective gender-neutral criteria of our internal compensation structure. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "professional / experienced" ;
